        "Hybrid Search",
        "Hybrid Search"
      ],
      "generation": {
        "attempted": true,
        "success": true,
        "provider": "groq/openai/gpt-oss-20b",
        "answer": "Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF) merges two ranked lists by using each document\u2019s rank position rather than its raw score. For each document, RRF assigns a score that is the reciprocal of its rank (e.g., 1/(rank\u202f+\u202fk)), then sums these scores across the lists. The resulting ranking prioritizes documents that appear high in any list, avoiding the need to normalize incomparable similarity or BM25 scores (Hybrid Search; DocuMind Project).\n\nSources: (Note: Hybrid Search), (Note: DocuMind Project)",
