        "attempted": true,
        "success": true,
        "provider": "groq/openai/gpt-oss-20b",
        "answer": "Heading\u2011based chunking works well for an Obsidian vault because:\n\n- Obsidian notes are written in Markdown, so headings (`#`, `##`, etc.) naturally delimit logical sections. Splitting at these boundaries keeps each chunk a coherent part of the note .  \n- Most Obsidian notes are short and single\u2011topic, so using a heading (or the whole note if it\u2019s short) as a chunk preserves the note\u2019s intent without fragmenting sentences or ideas .\n\nSources: (Note: Chunking Strategies), (Note: Obsidian RAG Assistant Project)",
